[1557.757566,"o","\u001b[1d\u001b[K\u001b[2;5Hsensitivity.\u001b[3;5H\u001b[1mI interpret interaction p-values only\u001b[m\u000f \u2014 never \"signific\u001b[Cnt in subgroup X.\" A\u001b[Cwithin-subgroup\u001b[CCI\u001b[4;5Hcro\u001b[Csing 1 means\u001b[Cthat\u001b[Csubgroup\u001b[Cis\u001b[Csmall,\u001b[Cnot\u001b[Cthat\u001b[Cthe\u001b[Cdrug\u001b[Cstops\u001b[Cworking.\u001b[5;5H\u001b[1mMultiplici\u001b[Cy:\u001b[m\u000f 9 tests, Bonferroni \u03b1 =\u001b[C0.05/9 = \u001b[1m0.0056\u001b[m\u000f. Wi\u001b[Ch 9\u001b[Ctests at\u001b[Cnominal 0.05 I expect\u001b[C\u001b[1m~0.4 \u001b[6;5Hfalse positives by chance alone\u001b[m\u000f, so one \"hi\u001b[C\" at p\u22480.03 is\u001b[Cnoise\u001b[Cuntil proven\u001b[Cotherwise.\u001b[7;5H\u001b[1mReporting floor:\u001b[m\u000f a subgr\u001b[Cup level\u001b[Cneeds \u2265\u001b[C0 patients and \u226520 death\u001b[C, else \"\u001b[Cot\u001b[Cestimable.\"\u001b[K\u001b[8;3H-\u001b[C\u001b[1mNo data-driven cutpoints.\u001b[m\u000f Age splits at\u001b[C65, AFP at 40\u001b[C \u2014 the conve\u001b[3Conal thresholds, not\u001b[Cwhatever\u001b[9;3H \u001b[Cmaximizes a difference.\u001b[K\u001b[10;5H\u001b[1mThe list is closed.\u001b[m\u000f Whatever comes out,\u001b[CI don't\u001b[2Cdd a 10th.\u001b[K\u001b[11;5H\u001b[K\u001b[12;3HRunning.\u001b[K\u001b[14;3H\u001b[38;5;246mRan \u001b[?25l\u001b[m\u000f"]
